<title>UK: Utd Utilities says wins 95-yr Argentina deal.</title>
<headline>Utd Utilities says wins 95-yr Argentina deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Utilities Plc, the UK electricity company, confirmed on Tuesday it had won a 95 year concession to run the biggest electricity distribution company in Buenos Aires, Argentina.</p>
<p>It is part of a consortium which includes Camuzzi and Loma Negra. United has a 45 percent interest in the consortium which won with an offer of $404 million.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
